              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_table_3.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>x</td><td>- 2</td><td>-1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>y = x<sup>2</sup> - 3x - 4</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>- 4</td><td>- 6</td><td>- 6</td><td>- 4</td><td>0</td><td>6</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.251,
            0.424,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we locate the points listed above on a graph paper and draw the graph, it will actually look like the one given in Fig. 2.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.339,
            0.424,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In fact, for any quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2}+bx+c,a\\ne 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the graph of the corresponding equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x ^ { 2 } + b x + c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " has one of the two shapes either open upwards like or open downwards like "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\triangle"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " depending on whether "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a > 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a < 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . (These curves are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "parabolas",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ".)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.538,
            0.425,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can see from Table 2.1 that –1 and 4 are zeroes of the quadratic polynomial. Also note from Fig. 2.2 that –1 and 4 are the x-coordinates of the points where the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = x ^ { 2 } - 3 x - { \\overline { { 4 } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " intersects the x- axis. Thus, the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 } - 3 x - 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are x-coordinates of the points where the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = x^{2} - 3x - 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " intersects the x-axis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.431,
            0.258,
            0.896,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.431,
                0.258,
                0.896,
                0.727
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.619,
                0.735,
                0.705,
                0.755
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.79,
            0.901,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This fact is true for any quadratic polynomial, i.e., the zeroes of a quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2}+bx+c,a\\ne 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , are precisely the x-coordinates of the points where the parabola representing "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x ^ { 2 } + b x + c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " intersects the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - \\mathrm { a x i s }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.857,
            0.9,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From our observation earlier about the shape of the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x ^ { 2 } + b x + c ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the following three cases can happen:"
            }
          ]
        },
